Title: Hallow-Eve
Order: 3
Production Code: 1x03

INT. VANCE ESTATE - DRAWING ROOM - NIGHT

AMB: a wood fire, young voices talking over each other

[[Molly Vance]] holds court before the fire, [[Aubrey Livingston]] leaning at the mantel, [[Charlie Vance]] sprawled on the sofa, [[Cora Scott]] and [[Reuel Briggs]] among the gathered friends.

MOLLY VANCE
Ghost stories, then — and better, let's try the charm ourselves. Tonight's the new moon. The lady of Hyde House only walks on a night like this one.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Bosh.

MOLLY VANCE
The bosh of a century, Aubrey. One at a time, into the avenue, a quarter hour each. Whoever waits long enough gets a prophecy.

Lots are drawn. Aubrey goes first and returns empty-handed at five past midnight. Charlie goes next, comes back rattled, having seen "a figure in the trees" and dared not wait.

CHARLIE VANCE
Your turn, Doc. Luck to you.

EXT. HYDE HOUSE - AVENUE OF HEMLOCKS - CONTINUOUS

SFX: wind through bare branches

Reuel walks alone under the hemlocks, more at peace than he's been in weeks — until a female figure resolves out of the dark ahead of him, walking toward him. Her eyes are wide, sorrowful, unseeing.

REUEL BRIGGS
You're in trouble, madam. May I help you?

She lowers the hands she'd been covering her face with. It's [[Dianthe Lusk]] — the singer from the Temple.

DIANTHE LUSK
(distant, calm)
You can help me. But not now. Tomorrow.

REUEL BRIGGS
Not now — but you're suffering. Shall I see you soon? Tell me —

She raises a hand. The gesture stops him where he stands. She turns and is gone among the trees.

He walks back to the house in a daze, and gives the others nothing but evasive half-answers about what he saw.
